    "title": "Lecture to relate life in internment camp",
    "text": "A Japanese man who was born in an internment camp during World War II will describe his experiences at 1:30 p.m. Wednesday, Jan. 28, at the golf course, 245 Conanicus Ave.\nThe presentation by Ken Nomiyama, who was born at Tule Lake, California, will describe how Japanese families from 1942-46 were racially targeted, forced from their homes and incarcerated in prison camps. He also will question whether history is repeating itself.\nRegister by contacting Eileen Donnelly at 401-423-9806 or edonnelly@jamestownri.net. The department of senior services is sponsoring this presentation at its temporary clubhouse site.",
